1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,500
We are Phobos Phantoms OG 7.66.

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:05,000
Our challenge: Interplanetary Survival Guide, Martian Map.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,500
This is Marswalk: plan, check and rehearse
the first human walk on Mars.

4
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:13,000
Real NASA HiRISE terrain of Jezero Crater:
1.5 by 1.5 km on a 2-metre grid.

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Our AI model reads the orbital photo and marks hazards,
checked on held-out ground.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,000
A planner links five science stops in 4.4 km,
always keeping at least 136 minutes to walk back.

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
In a Quest 3, the crater lands on your desk.

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Step in, and walk it at full size.

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
The visor shows walk-back margin, slope,
AI hazard and sun height at every step.

10
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Voice callouts and a controller buzz
warn of steep or hazardous ground.

11
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,500
Perseverance drives its real path beside you,
sols 405 to 717.

12
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:47,000
Press "Get me home": the live planner
routes you back around hazards.

13
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Checked against Perseverance's real track:
closer than a straight line, on gentler ground.

14
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Next: rehearse real EVAs before the first crews land.

15
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,500
Try it now, no login needed.
